","event_uuid":"818d9e32-e053-41c0-913d-8b7241b68581","position":{"commit_sha":"ab9d0f28c7b0c5476c934f90057c1d05c78f3436","position":"1786810007637680001-818d9e32-e053-41c0-913d-8b7241b68581"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"aa1208e7270a0938362452bfeb0466924fffff19a692a58d6d1551879c311917","event_uuid":"1f846a4d-1de0-47c2-b40f-bb792b140e71","position":{"commit_sha":"4a6556ce60519953bcba9fa87e5fd29c01a22487","position":"1786810324965304268-1f846a4d-1de0-47c2-b40f-bb792b140e71"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete in worktree ../deps-bump. Bumped pypandoc-binary 1.15->1.17 (wiki+dev) and ruff 0.16.1->0.16.2 (dev); mcp stays >=1.28.1,<2 / 1.29.0 — the 2.0 half of PR #127 remains deferred to epic 732b-51df-acf2-477b (bared-nickel-insect), consistent with PRs #124/#125. pypandoc-binary 1.17 bundles pandoc 3.9 (was 3.6.1): updated NOTICE, notice-test version string (upstream-URL assertion line untouched — owned by a parallel change), test_wiki_render.py provenance asserts (pypandoc 1.17 / banner 'pandoc 3.9'), ADR 0095 Pin provenance, ADR 0096 fingerprints, wiki_render.py docstring, tests/scripts generator-test literals (6). Byte-safety baseline re-established: LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION=3.9; darwin-arm64 sha256 d7b1e75cd20ee6a788a1399492be07d4559949e18e55f34cfc5c91807fdfa90d (installed binary); linux-x86_64 sha256 decd3dd11a3fe0c16ce56443343ec53adde6fbed6f97d7f56f06b1c424248e7b (extracted from the uv.lock-pinned manylinux wheel, wheel sha verified against uv.lock). Regenerated legacy manifest + 3 replay fixtures via the generator; diffs are provenance-only — pandoc 3.9's jira writer emits byte-identical output for all 884 units (smoke-verified shapes first: h1. {anchor:}, {{mono}}, arrow escaping, HTML-comment deletion all unchanged). Gates: generator --check PASS; targeted modules (notice/wiki_render/hardening/generator tests) 83/83 PASS; make lint (ruff 0.16.2, no new findings) PASS; make typecheck PASS; uv lock --check PASS. Full pytest tests/unit tests/scripts: 11516 passed, 43 failed + 13 errors — ALL pre-existing host-environment failures (git 'fatal: not in a git directory' on bare-repo config in test fixtures), reproduced identically on the untouched main checkout at origin/main 0f34e8dc3b; none touch pandoc/wiki/ruff surfaces. Proceeding to commit + push to Gerrit.","timestamp":1786809905366065001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed to Gerrit as change 1812 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1812), commit 88fad3f307, Change-Id Idfcf949fdec12e26b80fed93d5d91a57a9c6aac1, rebar-ticket trailer dc89-cd11-acd6-4e61 + DCO sign-off. AC1/AC2 verified (pins + lock, uv lock --check green, mcp stays 1.29.0 under <2). AC3/AC4 verified (all pin-provenance consumers at pandoc 3.9 / pypandoc-binary 1.17; baseline regenerated, generator --check green, hardening+provenance modules green). AC5: lint/typecheck green; pytest tests/unit 11516 passed with 43F/13E all pre-existing host-env git failures reproduced identically at origin/main 0f34e8dc3b (documented in prior comment). AC6 met by this push. AC7: mcp 2.0 NOT landed — deferral to epic 732b-51df-acf2-477b (bared-nickel-insect) recorded here; no edits to mcp constraints, _optionality.yml, or ADR 0050. Ticket stays in_progress while the orchestrator shepherds LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; close only after Submit/merge, then close GitHub PR #127 with a provenance comment pointing the mcp half at 732b.","timestamp":1786810007637680001}],"created_at":1786764663406395001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1f846a4d-1de0-47c2-b40f-bb792b140e71","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5f45-b951-5da4-4ae7"}],"description":"# Land PR #127 via Gerrit: pypandoc-binary 1.17 + ruff 0.16.2; mcp 2.0 deferred to 732b\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nGitHub is a read-only mirror: dependabot PRs never merge there; content is re-applied\nlocally and landed via Gerrit, then the PR is closed by hand. PR #127 proposes:\n`pypandoc-binary` `1.15` -> `1.17` (pinned EXACTLY, `wiki` extra + `dev` group);\n`ruff` `0.16.1` -> `0.16.2` (pinned EXACTLY in `dev` — hook, local lint, CI identical);\nand `mcp` `1.29.0` -> `2.0.0` (major), loosening the pyproject ceiling `<2` -> `<3`.\n\nThe `mcp` half is the THIRD re-proposal (PRs #124/#125/#127), rejected on evidence under\nticket 1dfd (mcp 2.0 removes `mcp.server.fastmcp`, imported by `src/rebar/mcp_server.py`\nand `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`); the migration is open epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b`\n(bared-nickel-insect): stay on `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` until 2.0.x stabilizes. PR #125 applied\nthe same rule (change 1483). This ticket lands the safe subset only.\n\n## Approach\n\nLand the `pypandoc-binary` + `ruff` bumps; the `mcp` ceiling stays `<2`. In a fresh\nworktree branched from `origin/main`:\n\n1. `pyproject.toml`: `pypandoc-binary==1.15` -> `==1.17` in BOTH `wiki` and `dev`;\n   `ruff==0.16.1` -> `==0.16.2` in `dev`. Keep both pins exact.\n2. `uv lock --upgrade-package pypandoc-binary --upgrade-package ruff` — the lock is\n   regenerated by uv, never hand-edited (CI gates on `uv lock --check`); sync the venv.\n3. **Pin-provenance consumers**: read the new BUNDLED pandoc version empirically\n   (`pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()`), then update EVERY hard-coded pin site (inventory:\n   `grep -rn '3\\.6\\.1|1\\.15'` over the whole tree, excluding only uv.lock and captured\n   fixture data):\n   * `NOTICE` — the `Version:` line + the `pypandoc-binary==1.15` wheel reference; and\n     the `\"3.6.1\" in text` assertion in `tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py`.\n     Do NOT touch its upstream-URL assertion (`\"pandoc.org\" in text or ...`) — a\n     parallel change owns that exact line.\n   * `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py` — NON-skipping provenance asserts\n     `pypandoc.__version__ == \"1.15\"` (L55) + banner `pandoc 3.6.1` (L59), and ADR\n     asserts `\"3.6.1\" in adr` / `\"1.15\" in adr` (L326-327).\n   * ADR 0095 — the \"Pin provenance\" pin + bundled-pandoc line (what L326-327 read);\n     conversion shapes re-verified by the module's real-pandoc shape tests (shape drift\n     = baseline churn, step 4 stop rule).\n   * ADR 0096 — the Finding recording the pins + both fingerprints (lockstep with 4b).\n   * `wiki_render.py` module docstring's `pandoc 3.6.1` mention (accuracy only).\n   * `tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` — passes hard-coded \"3.6.1\"\n     to `validate_pandoc_provenance` against provenance built from\n     `generator.LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` (L103/111/193/201/203/247); after 4a the\n     version-match check raises — update the literals (or derive from the constant).\n   `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/code_arrow.json` mentions the old pins too but is\n   captured historical ticket data — leave it byte-identical.\n4. **Byte-safety corpus**: `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` freezes\n   `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION = \"3.6.1\"` + a per-platform `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256`\n   map (darwin-arm64, linux-x86_64); test_wiki_render_hardening.py's provenance test\n   validates the installed binary's version + SHA-256 against the provenance in\n   `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.json` + the three replay files. Bumping the\n   wheel = deliberately re-establishing the reviewed baseline (sanctioned by the\n   generator's docstring):\n   a. Update `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` to the new bundled version.\n   b. Recompute BOTH fingerprints: darwin-arm64 = SHA-256 of the locally installed\n      pandoc; linux-x86_64 = download the exact 1.17 manylinux x86_64 wheel recorded\n      (URL + hash) in `uv.lock`, extract, hash the `pandoc` inside — no Linux host\n      needed; wheel integrity is attested by uv.lock.\n   c. Regenerate the legacy manifest + three replay files with the generator (supported\n      binaries of one version emit byte-identical fixtures, so a darwin regeneration is\n      valid for CI's linux gate; the provenance test enforces this).\n   d. Confirm with the script's non-writing `--check` + test_wiki_render_hardening.py.\n   If the bytes churn implausibly (unit count deviates from 884, or `--check` disagrees),\n   STOP: defer the pypandoc half too (land ruff alone) rather than commit an unreviewed\n   baseline.\n5. **ruff verdict drift**: run `make lint`; if 0.16.2 flags or reformats existing code,\n   apply the minimal fix and note it in the commit message. NEVER touch\n   `.github/complexity-baseline.json`.\n6. Do NOT touch the `mcp` constraints, `_optionality.yml`, or ADR 0050 — 732b's edit-set.\n7. Verify (`make lint && make typecheck`, `pytest tests/unit tests/scripts`, generator\n   `--check`), commit with a `rebar-ticket:` trailer + DCO sign-off, push\n   `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`; leave the ticket `in_progress` while the bots\n   vote; close only after merge, with PR #127 closed by a comment pointing at 732b.\n\n## Scope\n\n* `pyproject.toml` — the two `pypandoc-binary==` pins (`wiki` + `dev`) + the `dev`\n  `ruff==` pin.\n* `uv.lock` — regenerated entries + incidental churn.\n* Pin-provenance consumers (step 3): `NOTICE`, notice test (version string only, never\n  the upstream-URL line), test_wiki_render.py pin asserts, ADR 0095 \"Pin provenance\" +\n  ADR 0096 pin/fingerprint findings, `wiki_render.py` docstring,\n  `tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` version literals.\n* `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` — `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` + both\n  `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` entries, nothing else.\n* `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.json` + three `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_replay/`\n  files — regenerated wholesale by the generator, never hand-edited.\n* Minimal source fixes ONLY if ruff 0.16.2 changes a lint/format verdict.\n* OUT: the `mcp` bump and its `<2` -> `<3` ceiling move (deferred to epic\n  `732b-51df-acf2-477b` — already filed, no new ticket needed);\n  `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`; ADR 0050; `.github/complexity-baseline.json`;\n  dependabot config; other open dependency PRs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `pyproject.toml` has `pypandoc-binary==1.17` (twice), `ruff==0.16.2`, and\n  still `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` in both places\n  (`grep -nE 'pypandoc-binary==|ruff==|mcp>=' pyproject.toml`).\n- [ ] AC2: `uv.lock` records pypandoc-binary 1.17, ruff 0.16.2, mcp 1.29.0\n  (`grep -A1 -E '^name = \"(pypandoc-binary|ruff|mcp)\"$' uv.lock`); `uv lock --check`\n  exits 0 (CI's gate).\n- [ ] AC3: every pin-provenance consumer names the versions 1.17 actually ships (per\n  `pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()`): `NOTICE`, the notice test's version string,\n  test_wiki_render.py's provenance asserts, ADR 0095 Pin provenance, ADR 0096\n  fingerprints; `pytest tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py` exits 0 (non-skipping).\n- [ ] AC4: baseline re-established: `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` + both fingerprints match\n  the 1.17 wheels (darwin from the installed binary, linux from the uv.lock-pinned\n  manylinux x86_64 wheel), fixtures regenerated by the script (never hand-edited),\n  `python scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py --check` exits 0, and\n  `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py` exits 0.\n- [ ] AC5: `make lint` (ruff 0.16.2), `make typecheck`, `pytest tests/unit`, and\n  `pytest tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` all exit 0 with the\n  worktree `.venv/bin` first on PATH.\n- [ ] AC6: a Gerrit change carrying this diff exists on refs/for/main with this\n  ticket's `rebar-ticket:` trailer and DCO sign-off (`git log -1 --format=%B HEAD`).\n- [ ] AC7: mcp 2.0 NOT landed (no edit to the `mcp` constraints, `_optionality.yml`, or\n  ADR 0050 per `git diff origin/main --stat`); deferral recorded as a ticket comment\n  naming epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"bump pypandoc-binary==1.15 -> 1.17 (wiki extra + dev group) and ruff==0.16.1 -> 0.16.2 (dev group); mcp ceiling stays <2"},{"path":"uv.lock","reason":"regenerated by uv lock --upgrade-package for pypandoc-binary and ruff; mcp stays 1.29.0"},{"path":"NOTICE","reason":"update bundled pandoc version and pypandoc-binary wheel reference (bundled pandoc changes with the 1.17 wheel)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py","reason":"update the bundled-pandoc version-string assertion only; upstream-URL assertion line untouched (owned by a parallel change)"},{"path":"scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py","reason":"re-freeze LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION and both SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256 fingerprints to the 1.17 wheels (darwin from installed binary, linux from the uv.lock-pinned manylinux wheel)"},{"path":"tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.json","reason":"golden legacy manifest regenerated wholesale by scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py under the new pandoc"},{"path":"tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_replay/","reason":"three replay fixture files regenerated wholesale by the generator under the new pandoc"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","5f45-b951-5da4-4ae7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a6ecb3c1-b933-4d5b-a68b-3f9657469456","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"dc89-cd11-acd6-4e61","ticket_type":"task","title":"Land dependabot PR #127 through Gerrit: pypandoc-binary 1.17 + ruff 0.16.2 (mcp 2.0 deferred to 732b)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e616736c-2ef9-4b92-9669-64355e5c0622","31e1e8e7-17d1-42a3-9ea1-a33807a16a28","d1a095b6-b895-4975-877e-9230b6e8cea4","6800d12f-cd76-435c-887d-cbd3e5ecfa73","a69c3b87-3c12-4daf-8cd0-009edec7ac7d","b5b94ac6-8fcd-445a-9b77-14e54dad152e","1db0e404-b621-429f-961a-96159ca7c39d","5e8e4953-1178-4e3b-a5e5-1a199008cb5a","be566462-5fb7-4203-9bd5-b4251cb23910","cc0811e9-c188-4583-a1b6-c8d781e859b4","6d895049-55d1-49c4-9c5d-8593bad7eb31","f5d91617-3c3d-40af-95b3-a42d19224a16","31bc2698-6eea-42e9-b469-90a2a951856d","a6ecb3c1-b933-4d5b-a68b-3f9657469456","39c897ad-cebe-4d45-a7cc-2cd03c360d27","13492e2b-abf9-4455-868b-34cfcf5bc4e0","818d9e32-e053-41c0-913d-8b7241b68581","1f846a4d-1de0-47c2-b40f-bb792b140e71"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786810324965304269,"uuid":"afbf60a0-1e7e-4f6c-8c88-f0091459dbe2"}